<div class="wrap sec"><div class="prose narrow">
  <p>I am {{ site.author }}, a {{ site.role }} with 15 years in enterprise IT. Most of that time has gone into the platforms that deliver desktops and applications to users: Citrix, Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365, on premises, in hybrid setups and in the cloud.</p>
  <p>The projects were for large enterprise organizations. I have designed and implemented Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops (CVAD) and Citrix DaaS, including Workspace Environment Management (WEM), and architected, designed and implemented Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365. The end-user computing platforms I have worked on serve more than 18,000 users, and I led a Citrix to Azure Virtual Desktop migration of more than 2,000 users.</p>

  <h2>Citrix</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Design and implementation of Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops (CVAD) and Citrix DaaS for enterprise organizations.</li>
    <li>Hybrid estates where Citrix DaaS runs together with on-premises Delivery Controllers.</li>
    <li>StoreFront, NetScaler/ADC and NetScaler Gateway for internal and remote access.</li>
    <li>Workspace Environment Management (WEM) for managing user sessions and resources.</li>
    <li>Hosting on Azure, on Google Cloud VMware Engine (GCVE) and on on-premises VMware, including moving persistent VDIs between hosting platforms.</li>
    <li>Migration from Citrix to Azure Virtual Desktop.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Azure Virtual Desktop</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Architecture and design for enterprise organizations: host pools, session hosts, images, scaling and networking.</li>
    <li>Identity design with Active Directory and Entra ID, including several Active Directory domains connected to one Entra ID tenant.</li>
    <li>FSLogix for user profiles and the profile storage behind it.</li>
    <li>Implementation with Terraform, and management with Nerdio Manager for Enterprise.</li>
    <li>Day-to-day operations and troubleshooting, from the user session down to the session host and storage.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Windows 365</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Architecture, design and implementation of Cloud PCs for enterprise organizations.</li>
    <li>Provisioning, images and networking for Cloud PCs.</li>
    <li>Device and policy management with Microsoft Intune.</li>
    <li>Management with Nerdio Manager for Enterprise.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Platform and automation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Hybrid Azure and AWS infrastructure, and architecture that spans more than one cloud.</li>
    <li>Azure landing zones, built with Terraform.</li>
    <li>Terraform, PowerShell, Python, Git and n8n workflows, including health-check tooling for the daily checks on Citrix and Azure Virtual Desktop environments.</li>
    <li>Daily health checks, troubleshooting, root-cause analysis and runbooks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>AI for IT operations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read-only MCP servers and a diagnostic agent for Azure Virtual Desktop and FSLogix that traces a user problem to its root cause.</li>
    <li>RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) over documentation, so a model looks things up before it answers.</li>
    <li>An n8n voice assistant that answers Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365 questions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p>I take a platform from architecture and design through implementation and into daily operations. My AI tools are read-only: they look at an environment and report, they do not change it. This site is where I publish the practical side of that work as step-by-step guides, diagrams and labs.</p>

  <h2>Certifications</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Microsoft:</strong> Certified Trainer (MCT), Azure Solutions Architect Expert, Azure Virtual Desktop Specialty (AZ-140), Azure Administrator Associate</li>
    <li><strong>Citrix:</strong> Certified Professional – Virtualization (CCP-V), Certified Associate – Virtualization (CCA-V), Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops 7 on Citrix Cloud</li>
    <li><strong>Nerdio:</strong> Nerdio Engineer</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
  <p>You can find me on <a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
